      "id": "document:packages/opencode/src/server/routes/instance/httpapi/AGENTS.md",
      "type": "document",
      "name": "AGENTS.md",
      "filePath": "packages/opencode/src/server/routes/instance/httpapi/AGENTS.md",
      "summary": "Route-authoring conventions for the Effect HttpApi layer: HttpApiBuilder.group patterns, SSE handling via handleRaw, the three-file endpoint wiring (groups/handlers/server.ts), request-scoped vs stable services, the OpenAPI self-referencing component workaround, and the differing envelopes of the /global/event and /event SSE endpoints.",
      "tags": ["documentation", "httpapi", "conventions", "api-design", "effect"],
      "complexity": "moderate"
    },
    {
      "id": "file:packages/opencode/src/server/routes/instance/httpapi/api.ts",
      "type": "file",
      "name": "api.ts",
      "filePath": "packages/opencode/src/server/routes/instance/httpapi/api.ts",
      "summary": "Composition root of the HttpApi surface: assembles RootHttpApi (control + global groups with auth and schema-error middleware), InstanceHttpApi (15 instance-scoped route groups), and OpenCodeHttpApi, and registers the SSE event schemas derived from the BusEvent/SyncEvent registries as additional OpenAPI schemas.",
      "tags": ["api-handler", "entry-point", "httpapi", "effect", "composition"],
      "complexity": "moderate",
      "languageNotes": "Purely declarative assembly: HttpApi.make(...).addHttpApi(...) chains compose the route tree, and the OpenAPI Event union schema is generated at build time from the BusEvent registry rather than hand-written."
    },
    {
